      "key":"role_independence_and_direct_entry",
      "statement":"Where independent assessment supports promotion, the assessor evaluates the exact live subject, authority paths, proof and installed state, not the constructor's summary. Independence is claim-relative and imposes no actor count. Direct constructor entry requires one capable context with sufficient existing work authority, exact intake and operation grant; no coordinating activation is required solely for appointment. Configuration selects coordination when material contexts, authority, capability or required independence need it, never merely because of a role or frame name. Direct entry preserves admission, the smallest lawful carrier, required assessment and reserved decisions; it permits bounded work and condition-based recording, not self-acceptance at another owner's boundary.",
