        {
          "end_line":691,
          "quote":"A material change to the operation, the\nsubject, the territory, the authority or the validity conditions requires\nthe affected binding to be resolved before effect.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FRoles%20and%20delegation",
          "start_line":684
        }
      ],
      "key":"result_recording_and_grant_continuity",
      "statement":"Only when applicable law requires no independent assessment and reserves no acceptance may the grant-holding constructor record the satisfied bounded result, evaluated conditions and evidence in the existing durable result surface without adding a carrier, appointment, review or recreated design view solely for completion. Recording waives no applicable condition, reports no unperformed evaluation and disposes no other owner's boundary. Required assessment or reserved acceptance remains required; discovered insufficiency withholds the dependent effect and returns the question to its owner. Carriers and profiles add only their carrier binding. Actual role transitions are recorded in the existing work carrier; status change alone requires neither a new grant nor rehashing an unchanged subject. Material operation, subject, territory, authority or validity changes require affected binding resolution before effect. A sequence-wide grant never lifts a configuration's non-mutation restriction on its coordinating role, including the cited Executive restriction.",
