      "key":"context_capacity_fit",
      "statement":"Before reading, measure selected context in the declared capacity's unit, bytes or tokens, over the selected execution binding's boundary; record measurement, capacity and comparison. Fit covers only that boundary; outside context is not measured and receives no fit claim. The step's fit judgment requires recorded complete active inputs or a supported upper bound including host-supplied context; without either it is indeterminate unless a counterexample such as measured excess establishes falsified. A correct task result retains its bounded standing but cannot supply missing fit. This conditional measurement applies whatever question the step governs, is not a budget or universal gate, and proves fit only; adequate attention requires actual-use evidence. Other envelope dimensions and time, spend and resource limits retain their own laws.",
