      "key":"exact_acquisition_and_question_scope",
      "statement":"Acquire declared inputs by exact identity. Absence from the materialised view permits neither reading elsewhere nor concluding source absence. Acquisition is neither admission nor another actor stage and grants no role, operation or decision; effectful work still requires an admitted contract. Acquire a serving derived surface whose sources are current; for another task or a stale, missing or question-insufficient surface, acquire the deciding owner sections declared in the exact selected basis. Candidate sources, version-line selectors and another basis cannot substitute. Read the selected material and actual subject and follow needed material-source and coupled-obligation references. Sufficiency is for the named question and material relations, never universal. Before dependent action, name missing bindings: no available frame declaring evaluation needs yields out_of_frame; an absent or unverifiable exact required basis yields admission_refused(basis) at admission or activation_refusal(basis) at activation. Handle coupled material that does not fit through the fit procedure. A standalone surface can decide only questions its own source members own; questions owned elsewhere or joining several owners return out_of_frame naming owners and require those members at current digests or a surface declaring every owner.",
