      "key":"activation_evaluation_and_prompt_boundaries",
      "statement":"The actor or assigning authority selects one capable frame or declared active configuration. Activation binds exact subject and basis and loads declared material relations and evidence sources as the referenced packet, never an undifferentiated workspace dump. If no lawful frame/actor pairing exists, missing declared material relation or capability yields out_of_frame; otherwise the applicable activation_refusal cause governs. Implied context cannot sustain work. Evaluation distinguishes semantic law, observation, inference and decision and records every result-changing assumption. Prompt construction starts from the highest live authority surface needed, projects current authority references, obligations, contracts, boundaries, proof expectations, fallback conditions and acquisition-selected material, including raw owners when required. It names an upstream unresolved authority gap before reading fallback context and excludes obsolete workaround prose.",
