          "start_line":971
        }
      ],
      "key":"admission_outcome_mapping",
      "statement":"For lawful admission and activation: activated → satisfied only with admitted contract and admission evidence, exact Z/R/required-edge semantics/basis/scope, finite unique closure, selected-context projection and activated_frame. admission_refused(authority) → out_of_frame when no admission mechanism or explicit human override admits the exact contract, or no authorised available durable result/evidence surface exists; name missing authority or surface and owner. admission_refused(basis) → invalid_basis when cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis, or named exact subject/basis, cannot support the contract; name that basis. closure_unresolved → invalid_basis for closure/projection defects, naming failing condition and open basis coordinates. out_of_frame → out_of_frame when no frame/actor pairing declares a needed relation or capability, or no fit option fits context to an envelope. activation_refusal takes its cause, predicate and core value from REFERENCE_FRAME §5, without local remapping. Refusal creates no step, frame activation or work result; return it to assigning authority or declared result carrier and never record it as construction availability or a step's stop.",
