        },
        {
          "end_line":1026,
          "quote":"A stop\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FConstruction%20availability",
          "start_line":1023
        }
      ],
      "key":"construction_availability_mapping",
      "statement":"The cause-selected mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation; wording, timing and preference cannot change it. candidate_ready → satisfied when exact candidate and transition evidence are available, establishing availability only. refused → falsified when governing prohibition or owner-valid construction refusal defeats construction, with that prohibition/refusal as counterexample. incomplete → falsified for candidate availability when the step stops without output because required evaluation was unperformed or undecidable on admissible evidence, or execution ended first; stop basis and residuals identify which. re_entry_requested(authority) → out_of_frame for a needed material decision outside the grant, naming owner. re_entry_requested(basis) → invalid_basis when activated basis no longer supports work. Both re-entry causes are recorded when present, with basis taking precedence. Performed evaluations keep their own results, including indeterminate; planned unperformed evaluations have no result and remain work-state residuals naming unfinished capability or execution. Incomplete assessment never falsifies an unassessed criterion or the assessed subject.",
