      "conditions":[],
      "exceptions":[],
      "grounding":[
        {
          "end_line":1044,
          "quote":"| `accept` | the candidate closes its declared cone and preserves every affected governing relation | satisfied |\n| `local_repair` | implementation or proof is locally defective while the governing relation remains coherent | falsified |\n| `re_enter` | the governing outcome, a requirement, an identity, a lifecycle, an authority, a public contract or the accepted design must change | invalid_basis |\n| `reject` | the candidate violates a governing relation or leaves an undisposed competing truth path | falsified |",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition",
          "start_line":1041
        },
        {
          "end_line":1064,
          "quote":"it prohibits repeating an\nunchanged failed construction relation as if iteration alone could close\nit",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F3.%20Step%20results%20and%20disposition%2FDisposition",
          "start_line":1062
        }
      ],
      "key":"disposition_mapping_and_reassessment",
      "statement":"Only the decision owner disposes; an assessor may recommend, but recommendation is evidence, never disposition. accept → satisfied when the candidate closes its declared cone and preserves every affected governing relation. local_repair → falsified for local implementation/proof defect with coherent governing relation; the defect is the counterexample. re_enter → invalid_basis when governing outcome, requirement, identity, lifecycle, authority, public contract or accepted design must change; re-enter the owning relation because the construction/assessment basis cannot support acceptance. reject → falsified for a governing violation or undisposed competing truth path, which is the counterexample. A repair creates a new candidate with its own results. Global correctness conserves every affected global relation without requiring whole-product proof in each local action. Repeated rejection at one unchanged boundary requires reassessment of frame altitude, causal cone, common components, design-versus-code placement and authority sufficiency. No rejection threshold, mandatory round count or review state machine is imposed; unchanged failed construction cannot be repeated as if iteration alone closed it.",
