      "key":"totality_policy_and_hard_stops",
      "statement":"Name next moves in advance for every non-satisfied result and admitted condition class, including unknown. Applicable ambiguity policy and risk appetite choose ambiguity outcomes; this section states no default policy and names SPEC_METHOD §5 as its owner. Hard stops are not optional policy choices and halt at their condition regardless of risk appetite. Typical, non-exhaustive classes are violated invariant/guarantee, absent required authority surface, missing declared executional/operational capability, undeclared irreversible side effect and explicit human-approval gate. A declared ambiguity takes blocked; other cases take a transition stop. Adding algebra values does not solve hanging calls, unsatisfiable demands or lost post-effect responses.",
