      "key":"refinement_composition_and_licensing",
      "statement":"Faithful refinement requires exact steps: each admitted input satisfying Pᵢ yields output satisfying Pᵢ₊₁, retains every applicable invariant, exposes other outcomes without coercion and satisfies the next step's domain/preconditions. Successful exact composition carries P₀ to Pₙ by induction, assuming outer-obligation coverage, valid local implications and legitimate authority; local passes do not establish those premises. Non-next-step transfer needs a declared adapter composed as a step or a specialised contract whose domain names the carried material and whose exact owner authority, context, basis, scope, preservation, loss, refusal and invalidation law are declared. Coupled required relations fit together in some step; unrelated obligations remain excluded; every affected seam includes its far side or explains nonparticipation. Every layer states and discharges preservation of the layer above. Refinement/rewrite requires a subject-owner licensing law, such as declared associativity, commutativity or equivalence; without declared laws only universally valid steps are admissible. Any unlicensed and non-universal step, and any refinement/rewrite relying on it, is inadmissible. Approximate steps state adequacy and an argued composite end-to-end bound; such composites are adequate only within that bound, never faithful. Fixed per-step tolerances alone do not establish composition bounds. A step neither exact nor approximate with the required adequacy and composite bound is inadmissible, as is reliance on it. Material-transition admission remains one complete semantic commit or none, including the cited ODD realisation.",
