      ],
      "key":"complete_admission_atomicity_and_basis",
      "statement":"Derive and validate completeness from authoritative inputs; caller/owner assertions of completeness, validity, prior admission or authority do not establish truth. Bind one exact admission-valid authoritative basis through admission. If validity/currentness can advance after preflight, require the declared predecessor/currentness commit condition or effect-free re-entry into derivation and validation. Participating owners bind equal bases or a design-declared coherent composite; independently valid mixed-basis judgments cannot combine. Validate every participant and join before any effect. No subset or nested constituent becomes admitted truth; failure/interruption admits the entire transition or none. Direct, supported composite and nested realisations preserve this law; partial results cannot replace an owner's derivation/validation and competing same-scope paths cannot establish transition outside the governing relation. Same-basis reconstruction and replay exactly reproduce enclosing relation, basis identity and complete semantic outcome/refusal. The law is false for asserted-only completeness, omitted relevant participant/join/seam, unidentified/stale/incoherently mixed basis, advancing currentness without condition or effect-free re-entry, premature effect, exposed subset, differing reconstruction or remaining competing authority.",
