      "key":"admission_qualification_cases",
      "statement":"An excluded threat alone creates no acceptance predicate or defensive-work requirement; scope expansion returns to its owner, while supported malformed inputs, stale state and effect boundaries keep checks. Direct cases derive, validate and admit the complete relation once. Every supported composite/nested constituent and owner boundary obeys the same law; unsupported forms need design-grounded not_applicable and no weaker/competing path. Reachable forged identity, membership, equality or authority is refused without effect; exclusion requires owning authority, not helper inability. Unresolved participant/join/seam/relation identity is refused without effect. Stale input is refused; preflight-to-admission advancement causes effect-free re-entry. Incoherent multi-owner bases are refused without effect. Competing same-scope paths cannot establish transition. Fresh process/reconstruction and exact replay reproduce relation, basis and complete outcome/refusal. After successful validation, observe interruption/failure at every materially distinct commit/publication boundary capable of exposing subsets, then reconstruct all or none. An indivisible commit unit requires established boundary and observations immediately on both sides. Final-participant validation failure is not post-validation atomic-failure evidence. A standing claim is false if any owner/supported boundary is omitted, any distinct partial-failure boundary lacks observation or coverage proof, a weaker helper/manufactured refusal is used, or reconstruction omits complete semantic comparison.",
